(vector (map (:db/id -1)
  (:adr/doc_type "adr")
  (:adr/id "adr-2609110800-a-generator-fallback-produced-a-selector-that-measured-nothing")
  (:adr/topic "q9-generator-ref-arity")
  (:adr/title "A generator fallback produced a selector that measured nothing, and amu check could not see it")
  (:adr/status "accepted")
  (:adr/date "2026-09-10")
  (:adr/deciders (vector "Jun Kawasaki" "Claude Opus 5"))
  (:adr/repos (vector "com-junkawasaki/root" "kotoba-lang/kotoba-lang" "kotoba-lang/com-accela"))
  (:adr/related (vector "adr-2609110700-as-int-is-the-only-i64-divergence-in-the-wave-1-cohort"))
  (:adr/body
  "## Context

`scripts/gen-whole-component.cljs` generates a whole-component port from the
oracle's own `entity-specs` table. Its docstring says why it exists: a hand port
carried a sibling's expand-oracle selectors into a repository whose entity table
has different fields, and four arms would have gone green measuring an empty
fold. Deriving every name from the spec table means \"that class cannot be
carried\".

For the TABLES that holds. For two blocks it did not.

## The defect

`cred-row` and `oracle-expand` were not regenerated. They were reached only by a
token pass, and that pass carried a fallback:

    [(:ref-field-2 canon) (or (second (:ref-fields f))
                              (first (:ref-fields f))   ;; <- this
                              (:ref-field-2 canon))]

When the target entity declares ONE ref, `ref-field-2` collapses onto
`ref-field-1`. A one-ref repository therefore got `childPartId -> projectId` on
top of `parentPartId -> projectId`.

Measured on the SHIPPED `com-accela` component:

- `cred-row` emitted `\"projectId\"` twice -- a duplicate JSON key -- alongside a
  `\"quantity\"` field no accela spec declares.
- `oracle-expand` selector 4, the `expand BOTH refs` case, asked for
  `\"projectId,projectId\"`.

## Why it was invisible

Run all six selectors of the compiled artifact:

    amu extract-native a.kexe --symbol oracle-expand --output oe.bin   # :offset
    KEXE_FUEL=100000000 kexe-loader oe.bin <offset> 1 aarch64 7,23 <sel>

    sel 0 -> 303754089      sel 3 -> 499508843
    sel 1 -> 499508843      sel 4 -> 303754089      <- identical to sel 0
    sel 2 -> 701086944      sel 5 -> 499508843

Selector 4 returns exactly selector 0's value. It cannot tell a fold that ran
twice from one that ran once. In `com-abb-robotics`, whose BOM genuinely
declares two refs, the same selector IS distinct.

**`amu check` answers `:ok true` either way.** Both objects are built with `jkv`
calls, so the compiler has no schema for them. A green check is not evidence
that a fixture is well formed, and neither the duplicate key nor the degenerate
selector was reachable from any type.

## Decision

Both blocks are generated from the spec table, and the `BOTH` selector exists
only when there is a second ref for it to be about -- when there is not, the
generated file says so in a comment rather than emitting an arm that duplicates
another. The fallback is removed rather than adjusted, and the evidence floor
now also refuses a surviving template ref-field name: previously the alias hid
exactly that signal by rewriting it into a real name.

## The control, which is the half that matters

Removing selector 4 everywhere would also make the symptom go away, and would be
a reduction rather than a fix. So the check is a pair:

    regenerate com-abb-robotics (BOM has two refs)
      -> selector 4 present, asking for \"parentPartId,childPartId\"
      -> cred-row carries BOTH ref fields
    regenerate com-accela (Permit has one ref)
      -> no selector 4, and the file states why

Same generator, two inputs, opposite outputs. Both regenerated components pass
`amu check :ok true`, and accela's compiled artifact now answers 991960698 for
selector 4 -- the unexpanded floor it shares with 1, 3 and 5 -- instead of
duplicating selector 0's 827109938, while 0 and 2 stay distinct so the oracle
still discriminates.

## What was deliberately not done

The components are not regenerated. The shipped ones were measured, and
replacing a measured artifact is a separate step that deserves its own run and
its own parity numbers. Regenerating `com-abb-robotics` today would rewrite 41
lines of code whose values are recorded.

## What this says beyond one generator

A generator that derives most of its output from data, and reaches the rest
through a token substitution, has two different reliability stories in one file.
The derived part cannot carry a stale name; the substituted part can, and will
do it silently, because a substitution that finds nothing to replace and a
substitution that replaces with the wrong thing produce the same exit code.

The generator's own docstring is the thing to read carefully here. It claimed
the carried-selector class was closed. It was closed for the tables it names and
open for the two blocks it does not, and nothing in the output distinguished
those two regions.")))
